## Ticket protocol ({{project.name}}; printed by `zouinify init --protocol` and pasted here by the human; changed only by hand)

1. Read `{{tickets_dir}}/WORKER_BRIEF.md` first, then `export TICKET_AS=<your ListAgents name>`: every mutating
   `{{tickets_script}}` command refuses without it, and every log line is signed with it.
2. One ticket, one branch, one worktree under `{{worktrees}}/`. Nobody develops in the main worktree; never `git stash`
   in a shared repository; commit with the trailer `Ticket: T-xxxx` and push after every commit.
3. Evidence, not claims: a test RED on base and GREEN on the branch, pasted into the ticket; an independent reviewer gets
   the diff, never the author's summary.
4. Only the ticket desk (`{{desk.name}}`) addresses the human, in its own window, one ask per message. A relayed answer
   settles work decisions; it is never the human's own approval for a `CLAUDE.md` or settings edit or for a permission
   prompt in your session.
5. Never, from any session, anything on the human-only list:
{{human_only}}
6. Trunk is `{{trunk}}`; {{prod_clause_brief}}.
<!-- zouinify:protocol end -->
